# Skills deliberately in no bundle. Read by scripts/sync-bundles.py (--check) and
# tests/test_structure.py. Names are one per line; '#' starts a comment.
#
# A new skill goes into a bundle (create bundle/<team>/skills/<name>/, run
# `python3 scripts/sync-bundles.py`), not into this file. Add to ROOT_ONLY only
# with a reason. LEGACY_UNBUNDLED is a frozen debt list: it only shrinks.

[ROOT_ONLY]
# "Root-only" = the skill's job is the full `tonone` root plugin itself, so it has
# no meaning inside a bundle, which is an already-scoped fixed subset.
#  - apex-profile writes `enabledPlugins` to choose which <agent>@tonone-ai
#    plugins stay on instead of the full roster; it needs lib/signals
#    (project-shape.js), which no bundle ships. apex-stats and tonone-onboard
#    are its roster-level siblings (usage stats before pruning, install tour).
#  - The 27 hub skills (skills/apex, skills/forge, ...) have no team/<agent>/skills
#    source; they are the root plugin's per-agent entry points. A bundle delivers
#    the agent through agents/<name>.md instead.
apex
apex-profile
apex-stats
atlas
buzz
cortex
crest
deal
draft
echo
flux
forge
form
helm
ink
keep
lens
lumen
pave
pitch
prism
proof
relay
spine
surge
tonone-onboard
touch
vigil
volt
warden

